# Ultimate Cursor Rules for Beautiful UI Spacing & Design

## 1. MANDATORY SPACING SYSTEM - NEVER SKIP THIS

### **Container Spacing (ALWAYS APPLY)**
- **Page/Section containers**: `p-6 md:p-8 lg:p-12`
- **Card containers**: `p-4 md:p-6`
- **Modal/Dialog containers**: `p-6`
- **Form containers**: `p-4 space-y-4`
- **Content sections**: `py-8 md:py-12 lg:py-16`

### **Element Spacing (REQUIRED)**
- **Between components**: `space-y-6` or `gap-6`
- **Between form fields**: `space-y-4` or `gap-4`
- **Between buttons**: `space-x-3` or `gap-3`
- **Between text elements**: `space-y-2` or `space-y-3`
- **Between sections**: `space-y-8` or `space-y-12`

### **Layout Spacing (ESSENTIAL)**
- **Grid gaps**: `gap-4 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8`
- **Flex gaps**: `gap-3` for horizontal, `gap-4` for vertical
- **Navigation items**: `space-x-6` or `gap-6`
- **Header/footer padding**: `px-4 py-3 md:px-6 md:py-4`

## 2. SHADCN/UI COMPONENT ENHANCEMENT RULES

### **Always Enhance Default Components**
```tsx
// BAD - No spacing
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    Content here
  </CardContent>
</Card>

// GOOD - Proper spacing
<Card className="p-6 space-y-4">
  <CardHeader className="pb-4">
    <CardTitle className="text-xl font-semibold">Title</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="space-y-4">
    <div className="space-y-2">
      Content here with proper spacing
    </div>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### **Required Component Spacing**
- **Button**: `px-4 py-2` (small), `px-6 py-3` (default), `px-8 py-4` (large)
- **Input**: `px-3 py-2 space-y-1` (with label spacing)
- **Card**: `p-4 md:p-6 space-y-4`
- **Dialog**: `p-6 space-y-4`
- **Sheet**: `p-6 space-y-6`
- **Tabs**: `space-y-4` between tab content sections

## 3. RESPONSIVE SPACING SYSTEM

### **Mobile-First Approach (MANDATORY)**
```tsx
// Always start with mobile spacing, then scale up
className="p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8"
className="space-y-4 md:space-y-6 lg:space-y-8"
className="gap-3 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6"
```

### **Screen Size Spacing Rules**
- **Mobile (default)**: Smaller, comfortable spacing
- **Tablet (md:)**: 1.5x mobile spacing
- **Desktop (lg:)**: 2x mobile spacing
- **Large screens (xl:)**: 2.5x mobile spacing

## 4. TYPOGRAPHY SPACING RULES

### **Text Hierarchy Spacing**
- **Headings**: `mb-4` (h1), `mb-3` (h2), `mb-2` (h3)
- **Paragraphs**: `mb-4` between paragraphs
- **Lists**: `space-y-2` for list items
- **Captions**: `mt-2` after images/content

### **Required Typography Classes**
```tsx
// Heading system with proper spacing
<h1 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Main Title</h1>
<h2 className="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Section Title</h2>
<h3 className="text-xl font-medium mb-2">Subsection</h3>
<p className="text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">Body text with proper line height</p>
```

## 5. MODERN DESIGN PRINCIPLES

### **Visual Hierarchy Through Spacing**
- **Increase spacing** between unrelated elements
- **Decrease spacing** between related elements
- **Use white space** as a design element, not empty space
- **Group related content** with consistent spacing

### **Professional Spacing Patterns**
- **Content max-width**: `max-w-4xl mx-auto` or `max-w-6xl mx-auto`
- **Section padding**: `py-12 md:py-16 lg:py-20`
- **Card grids**: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6`
- **Form layouts**: `space-y-6` for form sections, `space-y-4` for fields

## 6. COMPONENT-SPECIFIC SPACING RULES

### **Navigation Components**
```tsx
