  <Button type="submit" className="w-full">
    Sign In
  </Button>
</form>
```

## 7. SPACING QUALITY CHECKLIST

### **Before Submitting ANY UI Component:**
- [ ] All containers have proper padding (`p-4`, `p-6`, etc.)
- [ ] Related elements are grouped with consistent spacing
- [ ] Responsive spacing scales properly across breakpoints
- [ ] Typography has proper line-height and spacing
- [ ] Form elements have adequate breathing room
- [ ] Cards and containers don't feel cramped
- [ ] Navigation has comfortable click targets
- [ ] White space enhances readability, not clutters

## 8. FORBIDDEN PRACTICES

### **NEVER DO THIS:**
- ❌ No spacing classes at all
- ❌ Only using `m-1` or `p-1` (too cramped)
- ❌ Inconsistent spacing throughout the design
- ❌ No responsive spacing considerations
- ❌ Text touching container edges
- ❌ Buttons too close to other elements
- ❌ Buttons having no click action
- ❌ No visual hierarchy through spacing

### **ALWAYS DO THIS:**
- ✅ Start with generous spacing, then adjust
- ✅ Use consistent spacing scale (4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24)
- ✅ Group related elements with smaller gaps
- ✅ Separate unrelated elements with larger gaps
- ✅ Test on mobile, tablet, and desktop
- ✅ Use white space as a design feature

## 9. FINAL RULE: SPACING IS NOT OPTIONAL

**Every UI component must have:**
1. **Container padding** - Elements should never touch edges
2. **Element spacing** - Related items need breathing room
3. **Responsive scaling** - Spacing should adapt to screen size
4. **Visual hierarchy** - Spacing should guide the eye
5. **Professional polish** - Generous, consistent spacing throughout

**Remember: Beautiful design is 80% spacing and 20% everything else.**
